# Client ACLs are per-host, not the whole LAN subnet. Anything on
# 10.57.57.0/24 could previously mount every export below; combined with
# no_root_squash that meant any device in the house had root on the backup
# tree. Narrowed 2026-08-11 to the hosts that actually mount, verified
# against live nfsd peers first.
#
#   10.57.57.80        kubernetes-controlplane-1 (pve)
#   10.57.57.81        kubernetes-worker-1 (px-0) — added 2026-09-01
#   10.57.57.82/84     retired control planes, kept for a 3-node rollback
#
# Adding a client means adding its IP here, not widening back to /24.
/media/library                  10.57.57.80(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.57.57.81(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.57.57.82(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.57.57.84(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash)
