# Public Jellyfin library, on the SSD pool so streaming to friends never wakes
# the SAS array. Quota caps it at 400G so it cannot crowd out the VM disks that
# share rpool.
#
# Was ro until 2026-08-30, when radarr-public started writing the library
# directly. jellyfin-public still mounts it `readOnly: true`, which the kubelet
# enforces on the pod; writing would need CAP_SYS_ADMIN to remount, and the pod
# drops ALL capabilities. So the internet-facing instance is still read-only —
# by pod spec rather than by export, since both land on the same node and NFS
# options are per client, not per pod.
#
# Layout inside: Movies/ is what Jellyfin scans, downloads/ is qbittorrent's
# save path for the public category. Same filesystem on purpose, so radarr
# imports by hardlink and a seeding torrent costs no second copy.
/public/library                 10.57.57.80(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.57.57.81(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.57.57.82(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash) 10.57.57.84(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,no_root_squash)
